[38;5;16m[48;5;153m ☐ Approach [39m[49m

[1m[38;5;231mWhich storage approach should the design use?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mA: Versioned JSON blob (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mOne versioned key holding all preferences, with a defaults layer and storage-event cross-tab sync. Simplest to [39m
     [38;5;246mversion and migrate.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m B: One key per preference
     [38;5;246mIndependent keys per preference. No write conflicts between tabs, but harder to version and clear as a set.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m C: Blob + schema registry
     [38;5;246mApproach A plus per-preference declared defaults and validators. Strongest guarantees, most ceremony.[39m
